{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Sends a conversation and optional tool definitions to the configured LLM and returns {kind: text|tool_calls|error, content|tool_calls, assistant_message}. THE provider engine: LLM= in runtime/agent/botd.properties picks an arm, and each arm speaks its provider's own dialect - VLLM and OPENAI use the OpenAI chat-completions wire, ANTHROPIC uses native /v1/messages (x-api-key + anthropic-version, system as a top-level param, REQUIRED max_tokens, input_schema tools, tool_use/tool_result content blocks, thinking blocks replayed verbatim, no temperature, optional ANTHROPIC_EFFORT/ANTHROPIC_THINKING, prompt caching on by default), GEMINI uses native generateContent (system_instruction, safetySettings BLOCK_NONE, functionDeclarations, named blocks), OLLAMA uses native /api/chat (keep_alive, options). VISION: a message may carry an `images` array of image file paths (png/jpg/gif/webp, <=20MB; e.g. the chat's runtime/agent/uploads) - content stays a plain string and each dialect renders the file as base64 in its own envelope (OpenAI data-URL content parts, Anthropic image blocks, Gemini inline_data parts, Ollama images array); arms with no image form (LOCAL, custom LLM_CTL, CLAUDECODE) ignore the key and the delegate works from the path. Every dialect normalizes into the same OpenAI-shaped result, so callers are dialect-agnostic. Per-arm keys and <ARM>_HEADERS cover any auth scheme; any other LLM= value dispatches LLM_CTL=lib:ctl:cmd. Retries only 408/429/5xx/transport.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::command::Command;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\nuse crate::agent::msg::put::put;","params":[{"name":"messages","type":"JSONArray"},{"name":"tools","type":"JSONArray"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"ytohmk19f70b2c09ck7ce2","readers":[],"time":1788268284727,"username":"system","writers":[]}